{title: Joyful, Joyful, We Adore Thee}
{lyricist: Henry van Dyke}
{composer: Ludwig van Beethoven}
{meta: arranger Edward Hodges}
{year: 1907}
{meta: tune-year 1824}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{meta: tune HYMN TO JOY}
{meta: meter 8.7.8.7 D}
{meta: variation The hymn, sung to HYMN TO JOY}
{meta: license public-domain}
{meta: tags praise, joy, creation}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Joyful, [C]joyful, [G]we a[D]dore Thee,
[G]God of [C]glory, [G]Lord [D]of love;
[G]Hearts un[C]fold like [G]flowers be[D]fore Thee,
[G]Opening [C]to the [G]sun [D]a[G]bove.
[D]Melt the [G]clouds of [D]sin and [G]sadness;
[D]Drive the [G]dark of [Em]doubt a[A]way; [D]
[G]Giver [C]of im[G]mortal [D]gladness,
[G]Fill us [C]with the [G]light [D]of [G]day!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]All Thy [C]works with [G]joy sur[D]round Thee,
[G]Earth and [C]heaven re[G]flect [D]Thy rays,
[G]Stars and [C]angels [G]sing a[D]round Thee,
[G]Center [C]of un[G]bro[D]ken [G]praise.
[D]Field and [G]forest, [D]vale and [G]mountain,
[D]Flowery [G]meadow, [Em]flashing [A]sea, [D]
[G]Singing [C]bird and [G]flowing [D]fountain
[G]Call us [C]to re[G]joice [D]in [G]Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Thou art [C]giving [G]and for[D]giving,
[G]Ever [C]blessing, [G]ever [D]blest,
[G]Wellspring [C]of the [G]joy of [D]living,
[G]Ocean [C]depth of [G]hap[D]py [G]rest!
[D]Thou our [G]Father, [D]Christ our [G]Brother,
[D]All who [G]live in [Em]love are [A]Thine; [D]
[G]Teach us [C]how to [G]love each [D]other,
[G]Lift us [C]to the [G]joy [D]di[G]vine.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Mortals, [C]join the [G]happy [D]chorus,
[G]Which the [C]morning [G]stars [D]began;
[G]Father [C]love is [G]reigning [D]o'er us,
[G]Brother [C]love binds [G]man [D]to [G]man.
[D]Ever [G]singing, [D]march we [G]onward,
[D]Victors [G]in the [Em]midst of [A]strife, [D]
[G]Joyful [C]music [G]leads us [D]sunward
[G]In the [C]triumph [G]song [D]of [G]life.
{end_of_verse}
